# This is NO LONGER THE MECHANISM, and it must not be read as one. Bytecode used to appear INSIDE
# the payload the moment the kit ran — unclassed state sitting in what we call the portable kit —
# and this fence was all that stood against it. `kit.lock.json` now enumerates what ships, the
# interpreter no longer writes bytecode at all, and the lock REFUSES any path it cannot account
# for. What remains here is ordinary git hygiene for a developer's tree, nothing more.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
